TY  - JOUR
TI  - Tranexamic acid for the treatment of postpartum haemorrhage (HARBOUR): an international, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial
AU  - Example, Ada
AU  - Sample, Ben
AU  - Placeholder, Chiara
AU  - Specimen, Dara
AB  - BACKGROUND: Postpartum haemorrhage is a leading cause of maternal death. Tranexamic acid inhibits fibrinolysis. METHODS: In this randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, women with a clinical diagnosis of postpartum haemorrhage after vaginal or caesarean birth were assigned to 1 g intravenous tranexamic acid or matching placebo, in addition to usual care. The primary end point was death due to bleeding within 42 days. Results are reported separately for vaginal and caesarean births. FINDINGS: Death due to bleeding was less common with tranexamic acid, most clearly when treatment was given within 3 hours of birth. (HARBOUR ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT09900101.)
PY  - 2023
DO  - 10.5555/kittum.example.harbour
JO  - Illustrative journal of obstetrics
AN  - 99000001
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
TI  - Early intravenous tranexamic acid versus placebo in women with postpartum haemorrhage (ESTUARY): a multicentre, randomised, controlled, phase 2 trial
AU  - Sample, Ben
AU  - Instance, Eli
AU  - Demo, Farah
AB  - BACKGROUND: The effect of tranexamic acid on blood loss after birth is uncertain. METHODS: In this randomised, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial, women with postpartum haemorrhage were assigned to intravenous tranexamic acid or placebo in addition to usual care. The primary endpoint was blood loss within 2 hours of randomisation in the overall population. FINDINGS: Blood loss was lower with tranexamic acid. This study is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT09900202.
