TY  - JOUR
TI  - Early intravenous tranexamic acid versus placebo in women with postpartum haemorrhage (ESTUARY): mortality, transfusion, and results by mode of birth from a randomised, phase 2 trial
AU  - Instance, Eli
AU  - Sample, Ben
AU  - Demo, Farah
AB  - BACKGROUND: We report mortality, transfusion, and results by mode of birth from the randomised, placebo-controlled ESTUARY trial. METHODS: Women with postpartum haemorrhage after vaginal or caesarean birth were randomly assigned to intravenous tranexamic acid or placebo; results are given separately for vaginal and caesarean births. FINDINGS: Tranexamic acid reduced red cell transfusion, with the benefit concentrated in women treated soon after birth. This study is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT09900202.
