TI  - Tranexamic Acid, an Antifibrinolytic, Given Early to Women With Severe Postpartum Haemorrhage: A Single-Arm Feasibility Study
AU  - Demo, Farah
AU  - Placeholder, Chiara
AB  - PURPOSE: To report the feasibility of giving tranexamic acid within one hour of the diagnosis of severe postpartum haemorrhage. EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN: Women were enrolled in an open-label, non-randomized, single-arm study and received intravenous tranexamic acid. RESULTS: Early treatment was feasible in most women.
